<Page title="How we research products" description="The renter-first criteria RenterSmartHome uses to evaluate smart locks, cameras, thermostats, lighting and plugs.">
  <p>Every recommendation on RenterSmartHome goes through the same renter-first checklist. We combine manufacturer specifications and installation manuals, independent lab and owner reviews, platform compatibility data (Matter, Thread, Alexa, Google Home, Apple Home) and our own lease-safety criteria.</p>
  <h2>Our five renter criteria</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Install footprint.</strong> Adhesive, tension-mount, plug-in or swap-and-restore. Anything that needs drilling, rewiring or changing a landlord-owned lock is clearly labeled.</li>
    <li><strong>Reversibility.</strong> Can you return the unit to its original state in under 15 minutes with basic tools?</li>
    <li><strong>Portability.</strong> Does it survive a move: new Wi-Fi, new door, new outlet layout?</li>
    <li><strong>Subscription honesty.</strong> We note which features need a paid plan and what works free.</li>
    <li><strong>Ecosystem fit.</strong> We favor Matter-compatible gear so you are not locked into one assistant.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Keeping guides current</h2>
  <p>Products change quickly. We revisit guides regularly, update recommendations when models are replaced, and show the last-updated date on every article. Prices are never hard-coded because they change daily; use the "Check price" buttons for current pricing.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spotted something out of date? Email us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and we will review it promptly.</p>
</Page>
